// ProjectDeliveryS740 — Sprint 740: the shared helpers descend below the verbs - dcSharedHelpersDescendBelowTheVerbs, the tenth D0479 extraction and the second slice of dcKeelCliIsThinDispatch, chartered by D0479. Before this sprint no cmd_ body could leave keel-cli: each reached project discovery (keel-process), the hook ledger writers (keel-hooks), fork detection (keel-serve), walk_longest (a pub fn of keel-cli's own lib.rs) or the nine private argument helpers of main.rs. scripts/verb_homes.py is written to measure that claim - for every top-level item of main.rs, the members its body reaches and the least member that could hold it - and scripts/extract_seams.py moves the five seams: project discovery to keel_git::projects (keel_process::workspace keeps the gate and re-exports the names), the ledger writers and the slow-fire threshold to keel_write::ledger (keel-hooks drops keel-process), fork detection to keel_model::textscan (deck re-exports), walk_longest to keel-fs, and the argument helpers to a new member keel-args that depends on keel-git alone. D0512 records the placement rule (a helper every verb shares lives in the lowest member that reaches what it needs) and reverses D0511's clause that put discovery in the process layer and the ledger writers in keel-hooks; the rest of D0511 stands.. EXECUTE. 5 pts.
