ays already applied. cargo clippy --release --workspace --all-targets -D warnings clean; keel --help byte-identical to the pre-move render (cmp help_before740.txt, 15089 bytes); keel version's guard line unchanged (75: 66 hard-blocking, 9 warning-only); python scripts/modgraph.py --check (74 modules, 7 edges) and python scripts/module_home.py --probe hold and module_home names keel-git/projects.rs, keel-write/ledger.rs, keel-process/workspace.rs; no path under GUARD_SOURCE_FILES or GUARD_SOURCE_DIRS changes. Known-positive (pos740.py): verb_homes.py --check exits 1 naming exactly the three items that reach keel-cli's own modules. Known-negative (neg740.py): a pub use keel_process::workspace planted in members/keel-args/src/lib.rs fails cargo check -p keel-args naming the undeclared crate, lib.rs restored on every path. The DoD's known-positive was amended three times this sprint as the least-member rule was refined; the final text and the tree hold at every point."; }
