    verification sharedHelpersDescendBelowTheVerbsReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "0e7d347d-aca8-402e-85be-cb4ef97ccdb3"; :>> title = "Sprint 740 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-18"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Verifier receipt only: keel gate validate, check-engine, guard --no-receipt, sync-claude --check, the verify ladder with --probe-from naming this sprint's pair file (D0500), cargo clippy; the recorder writes this gate from the receipt. Three passes per D0172. Correctness: every moved test passes in its new crate (root_arg's in keel-args, the fork tests in keel-model, the walker tests in keel-git), every caller of a moved name resolves through a re-export (keel_process::workspace::, keel_cli::workspace::, keel_serve::deck::, keel_cli::walk_longest, keel_hooks::ledger_*) or main.rs's named import, and the binary's help and guard count are the pre-move ones. Honesty: the negative plants in keel-args' lib.rs and asserts the compiler names the crate the member must not know; the positive asserts the exact set --check names, not its count, so a helper added to main.rs that a verb shares would fail it as a fourth name; the pre-move claims in the DoD were read from a git archive of HEAD (head740), not remembered. Scope: no locked path is in the diff (GUARD_SOURCE_FILES and GUARD_SOURCE_DIRS in members/keel-guards/src/enforcement.rs unchanged, no moved file under them), no hook script, CI yml or rule edit, so D0512 carries no marker and accepted under standing consent - NOT A PROCESS CHANGE: every hook and verb fires the same body through a re-export."; }
