a file; fixed in the transform's rewrite of the doc. Not tracked: dual-truth in a comment with no lint, same class as 739's finding (4), and the moved fn now sits under a doc that says what it reads. (5) D0511 placed project discovery in the process layer and the ledger writers in keel-hooks one sprint before verb_homes.py existed to measure placement; D0512 reverses that clause with a #SupersedeClause edge and the rest of D0511 stands. Not tracked separately: the tool is now committed and its --check is the control; a placement Decision recorded before the tool ran is what D0388 (probe before the answer) already forbids, and dcKeelCliIsThinDispatch's DoD now cites the tool's table for every move. (6) verb_homes.py --check exits 1 on the tree and will until dcTheFourStayingModulesAreMembers lands, so it cannot be a CI gate yet and its # ci-probe marker runs only the fixture. Non-finding: the exit-0 gate is dcKeelCliIsThinDispatch's DoD, recorded this sprint, and the three named items are the next sprint's own seam. (7) issue601 was recorded with its resolver an existing item whose DoD was amended, rather than a new task appended at the end of EngineBuild - the issue600 shape (record task appends, then a hand move) was avoided by not recording a task. Non-finding, noted because it is a workaround for issue600 and not its fix."; }
